+
+## Viewing your data
+
+### How do I see where my money went?
+
+```
+python -m tally.cli report --month 2024-03
+```
+
+This prints category totals for the month. Add `--category food` to narrow it to
+a single category.
+
+### How do I see individual expenses instead of totals?
+
+```
+python -m tally.cli list --month 2024-03
+python -m tally.cli list --month 2024-03 --category food
+```
+
+### How do I get overall lifetime statistics?
+
+```
+python -m tally.cli stats
+```
+
+This prints the total number of expenses, the combined total in USD, the
+average per expense, and the date range they cover.
+
+### Can I export my data?
+
+Yes. The `export` command writes everything to CSV in US dollars:
+
+```
+python -m tally.cli export --out march.csv
+```
+
+Omit `--out` to write to standard output instead.
+
+---
+
+## Budgets
+
+### How do I set a budget?
+
+Monthly budget limits per category live in `CATEGORY_BUDGETS` inside
+`tally/config.py`. Edit them to match your own targets.
+
+### How do I check my spending against a budget?
+
+```
+python -m tally.cli budget --month 2024-03
+```
+
+The output shows each category's spending against its limit. A warning indicator
+appears once spending crosses 80 % of the limit.
+
+---
+
+## Data and privacy
+
+### Where is my data stored?
+
+In a single JSON file called `tally.json` in whatever directory you run the
+command from. Unless you turn on the optional hosted backup add-on, your data
+never leaves your machine.
+
+### Can I change where the data file lives?
+
+Yes. Pass `--store` with a path of your choice:
+
+```
+python -m tally.cli --store ~/finances/expenses.json add 12.50 food
+```
+
+You can also put your alias in a wrapper script that always passes the right
+`--store` path.
+
+### Can I back up or diff my data?
+
+Yes. The store is plain JSON, so any file-backup tool, `git`, or a plain `cp`
+works. The `export` command also gives you a CSV snapshot you can open in a
+spreadsheet.
+
+---
+
+## Plans and pricing
+
+### Is tally really free?
+
+Yes. Running tally on your own computer is free and always will be. The only
+thing that costs money is the optional hosted backup add-on.
+
+### How many expenses can I track on the free plan?
+
+Locally, there is no limit — you can record as many expenses as you like. The
+free plan for the hosted backup add-on covers up to **100 expenses per month**.
+If you record more, the extras are still saved locally; they are simply not
+included in the hosted backup until you upgrade.
+
+The Plus and Family plans remove the limit. See `docs/pricing.md` for the full
+comparison.
+
+### How long is backup history kept?
+
+| Plan | Backup history |
+|------|----------------|
+| Free | 7 days |
+| Plus | 1 year |
+| Family | 3 years |
